{
  "id": "30131_kizasu",
  "headword": "{兆|きざ}す",
  "reading": "きざす",
  "romaji": "kizasu",
  "part_of_speech": "verb (godan)",
  "gloss": "to show signs; to begin to appear; to sprout",
  "definitions": [
    {
      "sense_number": 1,
      "gloss": "to show signs; to begin to appear",
      "explanation": "For something not yet visible — a season, a feeling, a social change — to give its first faint indication. The subject is the thing coming into being, not the person noticing it."
    }
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "id": "30131_kizasu_ex1",
      "japanese": "{春|はる}が{兆|きざ}す。",
      "english": "Spring is beginning to show itself.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "30131_kizasu_ex2",
      "japanese": "{胸|むね}の{中|なか}に{不安|ふあん}が{兆|きざ}し{始|はじ}めた。",
      "english": "Unease began to stir in my chest.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "30131_kizasu_ex3",
      "japanese": "{長|なが}い{冬|ふゆ}が{終|お}わり、{野原|のはら}のあちこちに{新|あたら}しい{命|いのち}が{兆|きざ}していた。",
      "english": "The long winter had ended, and new life was beginning to appear here and there in the fields.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    }
  ],
  "notes": "A literary verb, most at home in writing about nature, moods, and social currents. The related noun {兆|きざ}し (a sign, an omen) is far more common in everyday Japanese: {回復|かいふく}の{兆|きざ}しが{見|み}える (signs of recovery are visible).\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\nIntransitive; the thing appearing is the subject and takes が ({不安|ふあん}が{兆|きざ}す).\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {春|はる}が{兆|きざ}す: for spring to show its first signs\n- {不安|ふあん}が{兆|きざ}す: for unease to stir\n- {芽|め}が{兆|きざ}す: for buds to start to appear\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {芽生|めば}える: to sprout; to bud — used both of plants and of feelings, and much more common\n- {現|あらわ}れる: to appear — neutral and general; the thing is already visible, not merely hinted at",
  "schema_version": "2.0",
